<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayapida</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Vinayaditya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayapida was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karkota-dynasty">Karkota dynasty</a> in the late 8th century, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitaditya-muktapida">Lalitaditya Muktapida</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajatarangini">Kalhana's Rajatarangini</a> he campaigned in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and was a generous patron of learning, with the grammarians and critics Vamana and Udbhata at his court. His later reign is described as oppressive.</p></div>
